course: dictionary
lesson: 14011
title: Macedonian in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Macedonian is a word about where something or someone comes from. Look at the words around it. «Mila's grandmother is Macedonian, and she was born in North Macedonia.» The sentence tells you the place, so Macedonian means from or to do with that place.
explain: The same word can name a language or a people. «We learned some Macedonian words in class.» Learned words is the clue: a language is something you can learn. «The Macedonians welcomed the visitors» is about the people. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: In history, the word can mean something from long ago. «Alexander the Great was a Macedonian king who ruled a huge empire.» The clue is king and empire, which tells you this is about ancient Macedonia, not the country today.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence: «Alexander the Great was a king from ancient Macedonia.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Macedonian means from or to do with Macedonia, its people, or its language.
fact: North Macedonia is a country in the Balkans. Its people and its language are both called Macedonian.
fact: The Macedonian language is a Slavic language, written in Cyrillic letters.
fact: Ancient Macedonia was a kingdom ruled by Philip II and his son, Alexander the Great.
fact: Macedonia is also a region of northern Greece, so Macedonian can mean from there too.
exercise: «Mila's grandfather came from North Macedonia, so she is Macedonian.» What does Macedonian mean here? | A kind of cake | Very old | *From North Macedonia | From the ocean
exercise: «The Macedonian language has its own letters, called Cyrillic.» What is the Macedonian language? | A language spoken in Japan | A type of music | A sport played in the Balkans | *A Slavic language spoken in North Macedonia
exercise: «Alexander the Great was a Macedonian king who ruled an empire long ago.» Which Macedonia is meant? | A village near the sea in England | *Ancient Macedonia, the kingdom of Alexander | Modern Germany
test: «The shop sells olives from Macedonia, a region of northern Greece.» Where do the olives come from? | Spain | *A region of northern Greece | The moon | North America
test: Why did North Macedonia change its name in 2019? | To celebrate Alexander the Great's birthday | It was a rule for all countries | *After a long disagreement with Greece about the word «Macedonia» | Because it joined the Olympics
exam: «Ana speaks Macedonian at home, and her grandmother tells Macedonian stories.» Which meaning fits Macedonian in «speaks Macedonian»? | *The Macedonian language | A Macedonian king | A kind of football | Greek food
